  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most important task is to establish a reliable baseline that anchors all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: PCA is a deterministic, untrained dimensionality reduction (no encoder hyperparameters to confound interpretation), singleprofile avoids aggregation complexity, and RNA-only isolates one modality. This gives us a clean reference for RNA performance that every other RNA-based and multimodal configuration can be compared against. It is also computationally cheap, so if it underperforms we quickly learn that RNA alone is insufficient and can pivot toward image or multimodal settings with less wasted budget. Testing this first reduces the largest source of uncertainty—what the individual-modality floor looks like—before we invest experiments in more complex multimodal or learned-encoder configurations."
}

